Base final clause: `not exists q in I+ and t0 in [0,T) with gamma([t0,T)) subset J^-(q) intersect M` — this is a co-binding: q ∈ I+, t0 ∈ [0,T), both variables bound by the same `not exists` quantifier whose scope is the "with" body.

Legal renderings (pos):
- `not exists (q,t0) in D5 with ...` — grouped tuple where D5 is presumably the product domain I+ × [0,T). Legal.
- pos_grouped_tuple_space: `(q, t0) in D5` — same, whitespace-only. Legal.
- pos_variablewise_double_space: `q in I+  and  t0 in [0,T)` — same co-binding, extra spaces. Legal.
- pos_such_that_grouped: `(q,t0) in D5 such that ...` — same. Legal.
- pos_filler_also: `q in I+ and also t0 in [0,T)` — same. Legal.
- pos_wide_whitespace: same as variable-wise with wide whitespace. Legal.

